    },
    "body": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Unit testing in JavaScript and React doesn't have to be something you dread. Personally, I enjoy writing unit tests for UI logic because it forces me to adhere to a more structured and well thought out format. When writing production code, that can be a godsend for comprehension later on by others or simply for your output speed. However, a lot of people find writing unit tests for React UIs to be daunting because of how much you need to tip-toe around the browser APIs or having to Mock hooks. That's why most people resort to snapshot tests 🙄, which while somewhat useful, don't assist in verification of frontend logic. \n\nLook at this simple todo list component: ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ],
          "data": {}
        },
        {
